  "id": "COMPOUND:14823 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Heparin is implicated in the regulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular interactions involving phosphodiesterase 6C. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence chains, all of which point to heparin as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The shared target of heparin with phosphodiesterase 6C suggests a potential role in modulating the activity of this complex, possibly through the inhibition of its downstream targets. The presence of multiple compounds with similar target profiles further strengthens the hypothesis that heparin may exert its effects by influencing the activity of phosphodiesterase 6C, which in turn could modulate the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The integrated evidence suggests a mechanistic link between heparin and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
